.TH SETITIMER 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
setitimer \- arm or replace a process interval timer
.SH LIBRARY
Substrate libc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <sys/time.h>

int setitimer(int which, const struct itimerval *new_value,
    struct itimerval *old_value);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR setitimer ()
replaces one of the calling process's interval timers.
If
.I old_value
is non-null, the previous timer state is returned before the replacement is installed.
.P
The
.I which
argument selects
.BR ITIMER_REAL ,
.BR ITIMER_VIRTUAL ,
or
.BR ITIMER_PROF .
The
.I it_value
field arms the timer; a zero value disarms it.
The
.I it_interval
field configures automatic reload after expiry.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success,
.BR setitimer ()
returns 0.
On error, it returns -1 and sets
.BR errno .
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I which
is unsupported, or one of the supplied
.B timeval
fields is negative or has a microsecond component outside the range 0 through 999999.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I new_value
or
.I old_value
does not reference accessible user memory.
.SH NOTES
In Substrate,
.B alarm()
is implemented in terms of
.BR ITIMER_REAL .
Replacing
.BR ITIMER_REAL
with
.BR setitimer ()
also replaces any pending
.BR alarm ()
request.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR alarm (2),
.BR getitimer (2),
.BR signal (2)
